      "issue": "The node claims the cause of the air-low indication is unknown because shift entries do not identify it. This conflates 'not identified in provided text' with 'unknown fact'. The evidence packet explicitly states that supporting records will be provided as investigation develops; thus, labeling this condition as a confirmed gap without additional data violates the instruction to avoid assuming absence.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Evidence of whether any diagnostic test (e.g., valve position log, compressor trip record) or witness statement identifies the interruption point. If none exist yet, the node must be marked 'unknown' with an explicit note that further records are pending.",
      "question": "Do any available logs, alarms, or maintenance tickets contain a specific fault code, sensor failure report, or valve state change at ~10:00 AM?"
    },
